From 6a0c9e3c1940c28dd50adb9f972e8b26db0a4c6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasilii Zolotukhin <vasilii.zolotukhin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:41:58 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] Mac: choice of the profile color mark, a line on top by
 default
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The mark that shows a tab's profile color in the unified tab strip is
now chosen in the tab and strip context menus (Profile Color ▸): a line
along the top (the default), the corner triangle, a line below, a bar
on the side, a corner outline, or none. The choice applies to all
windows and is kept in the <bundle id>.profile-tabs defaults
(ProfileMarkStyle).

All marks are clipped to the shape of the active tab's background, so
they follow its rounded top corners. Marks at the leading edge replace
the separator in front of the tab; the lines keep it.
